        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Factory/Droid API-key usage auth",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Add Droid usage source modes `Auto | API key | Browser cookies`, with Settings API key field and `codexbar config set-api-key --provider factory` / `FACTORY_API_KEY` / optional `~/.factory/.env` resolution.\n- Reuse the existing Factory bearer billing-limits path for API keys; Auto prefers API when a key is available and falls back to cookies/WorkOS on missing/unauthorized credentials.\n- Preserve API-host 401/403 across app-host fallback retries so Auto web fallback is not masked by later 404 noise.\n- Unify `FactoryStatusProbeError` cases for Linux CLI builds (ubuntu CI) and rename `FactoryApi*` → `FactoryAPI*` to match repo naming.\n\n## Deliberate notes\n- **Source modes:** Factory previously advertised `[.auto, .cli]` while only implementing a web strategy. This PR switches to `[.auto, .api, .web]` and **keeps `.cli` as an Auto compatibility alias** so persisted `source: cli` configs keep validating / dispatching (Settings UI still normalizes to Auto).\n- **Linux:** API-key bearer HTTP works on Linux CLI; browser-cookie/WorkOS remains macOS-only. Auto/cli skips the Linux web gate when a Factory API key is resolvable.\n- **Docs:** `docs/factory.md` corrects the subscription usage endpoint from POST to GET to match the probe.\n\n## Fork / prior review\n- Fork PR (reviews already addressed): https://github.com/araa47/CodexBar/pull/1\n- Rebased onto latest `steipete/CodexBar` main before opening this PR.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `make check`\n- [x] `swift test --filter 'FactoryAPI|FactorySettingsReader|applies API key override for factory|factory config'`\n- [x] CLI smoke: `CodexBarCLI usage --provider factory --source api` with `FACTORY_API_KEY`\n- [x] CLI smoke: `usage --provider factory --source web` without forcing API key\n- [x] Local `CodexBar.app` packaged/launched; Settings UI (Usage source + API key) checked\n- [x] Codex gpt-5.6-sol + Claude fable review findings addressed (Linux enum + API casing, 401/403 host fallback)\n- [ ] CI `build-linux-cli` on this PR\n",
        "branch": "feat/factory-api-key-usage",
